   "flags": {},
   "order": 10,
   "mode": 0,
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Character reference sheet (front, side, back)\n**VTube Pro workflow, 8 GB graphics card** (SDXL). Pack 2026.10.01.\n\nFront, side and back views of an original character, to model from or to paint textures with.\n\n## How to use it\n1. Describe your character in \"Your prompt\": hair, eyes, outfit, colours.\n2. Press Run a few times and keep the most consistent sheet.\n3. Find the result in ComfyUI's **output/VTubePro** folder (or right-click the picture > Save Image).\n\nThe **green boxes** are the ones to change.\n\n**You get:** One wide sheet, 2048x1024 PNG, plain background.\n\n**In VTube Pro:** Use it as the reference for the texture repaint workflow and for your model maker.\n\n**Settings:** 1536x768, 28 steps, CFG 5, then Real-ESRGAN to 2048x1024.\n\n## Models (all allow commercial use)\n- [animagine-xl-4.0-opt.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/cagliostrolab/animagine-xl-4.0) (6.9 GB) in `models/checkpoints`: CreativeML Open RAIL++-M\n- [RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged) (0.1 GB) in `models/upscale_models`: BSD-3-Clause\n\nMissing a model? ComfyUI offers to download it when you open this workflow. Or ask your AI: \n*\"Set up the VTube Pro character sheet workflow in ComfyUI\"*: the VTube Pro Helper downloads every file from its official page, checks it, and adds this workflow, after you say yes.\n\n## Tips\n- Original designs only: no existing characters, logos or game outfits.\n- A neutral A-pose and even light make modelling easier.\n- Make pictures when you are not live: picture AI slows face tracking."
   ],
   "title": "Start here",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
